From: Grokbot <grokbot@s-w.art>
Subject: arm64: dts: qcom: x1-asus-vivobook-s15: add top-level /sound graph

Port Elliot Huang's tested Vivobook S15 sound DTS (LKML 2025-06-02,
"arm64: dts: qcom: support sound on Asus Vivobook S15"; github copy
binarycraft007/linux-x1e80100-vivobook-s15) onto the 7.2 split board
file x1-asus-vivobook-s15.dtsi.

7.2 / mainline still ship SoC soundwire + WSA/TX/RX/VA macros under
soc (swr0/1/2 disabled; macros enabled) but the Vivobook board DT has
no top-level sound { } and no WSA/WCD children. ALSA therefore has
nothing to bind even after full ADSP.

This adds, matching Elliot's tested graph (2 WSA8845, WCD9385 jack,
2 VA DMICs, DP0/DP1 playback):
  * /sound compatible qcom,x1e80100-sndcard
    model X1E80100-ASUS-Vivobook-S15
  * wcd938x + swr0 speakers + swr1 RX + swr2 TX
  * pm8550 ldo1 (vreg_l1b_1p8) and ldo12 (vreg_l12b_1p2)
  * lpass_tlmm gpio12 speaker SD_N + WCD reset tlmm gpio191

Not a Yoga Slim 7x 4-speaker copy. T14s is the closer 2-speaker peer
(audioreach-topology PR #22 reuses the T14s topology under this
model name). Not a PAS -22 / qebspil AUTH fix: lite ADSP still has
no audio; topology + UCM are still required after this DTS.

Omarchy must still capture live DT (soundwire/WSA phandles, gpio
resets) if this board differs from Elliot's wiring.

Signed-off-by: Grokbot <grokbot@s-w.art>
